/**
	The number of the currently selected voice.
	int tts_voice::voice;
	## Remarks:
		This property is read-only; set_voice changes the voice. Until a voice is chosen with set_voice or set_language, this is the voice the engine speaks with, which follows the platform's settings as the user changes them (see voice_set). When that voice isn't in the list, one installed while the program runs for instance, the list is made again, so the voice numbers can change. It is -1 when the engine can't say which voice it speaks with, or that voice isn't in the list even then, as when a Siri voice is chosen in Apple's Spoken Content settings, which apps can't use or see, or on Android while the voice of the user's settings isn't installed, or when set_language left that voice's language out.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	tts_voice v;
	alert("Current voice index", v.voice);
	v.set_voice(0);
	alert("Current voice index", v.voice);
}
